THE KYANITE NAME AND LOGO ARE NOT FREE SOFTWARE
===============================================

Kyanite's *code* is released under a free software licence, in its own
repositories. This repository holds something different: the artwork and
the name that identify the project. They are reserved, and this file says
exactly what that means.

All rights in the designs, drawings, image files and source files in this
repository are reserved by the Kyanite project.


WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING
------------------------------

You may reproduce the logo, unmodified, to refer to Kyanite. For example:

  - an article, a review, a blog post or a talk about Kyanite;
  - documentation, a tutorial or a course that covers Kyanite;
  - a list of links, a directory, a distribution gallery;
  - a package repository or a mirror that distributes Kyanite itself;
  - a screenshot, or a system that has Kyanite installed on it.

This is nominative use: using the mark to name the thing it names. You do
not need permission for it, and you do not need to ask us first.

When you do, use the files as delivered: pick the variant that suits your
background rather than recolouring, and keep the proportions. The usage
notes in logo/README.md are guidance, not extra conditions.


WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
-------------------

  - Use the name "Kyanite" or this logo to name, brand or sign anything
    that is not the Kyanite project: a derived image, a product, a
    service, an application, a repository or an organisation.
  - Modify the logo and keep calling it the Kyanite logo.
  - Use either in a way that suggests the project endorses, sponsors or
    is affiliated with you, when it does not.
  - Register either as a trademark, or as a domain name or account name
    that would be taken for the project itself.


DERIVED IMAGES
--------------

Kyanite's code is free software, and you are welcome to build your own
image from it — that is the point of releasing it. But a derived image is
your project, not ours.

Give it its own name and its own mark. You may say truthfully that it is
"based on Kyanite" or "built from Kyanite"; you may not call it Kyanite,
nor ship it carrying this logo.


FONTS AND THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
------------------------------

The word in the logotype is set in Inter, by Rasmus Andersson, which is
licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Inter is not covered by the
reservation above; its own licence applies to it, and it explicitly
permits derivative works. The word is converted to outlines in the
delivered files, so no font is required to display them.


ANYTHING ELSE
-------------

For any use outside what is permitted above, ask. The project would
rather say yes to a reasonable request than have people guess.
